part.text:
Fixed. The bug was in `popGenericCommand` (src/db.c:197-205), which replied with a null bulk string (`$-1`/`_`) whenever the key didn't exist, even when a count argument was given. The fix replies with a null array (`*-1` in RESP2, `_` in RESP3) when `count` is provided, matching the documented behavior:

```c
robj *o = lookupKeyWrite(db, key);
if (o == NULL) {
    if (hascount) {
        /* Null array reply when count is provided, see LPOP/RPOP docs. */
        addReplyNullArray(c);
    } else {
        addReplyNull(c);
    }
    return;
}
```

Verified in the container: `LPOP k 10` now returns `*-1\r\n` (RESP2) / `_\r\n` (RESP3), while plain `LPOP k` still returns `$-1`. `unit/type/list`, `unit/multi`, and `unit/protocol` all pass.
